   "l": "to cast off frugality and go for breadth,\nto cast off the hindmost place and go for the front —\ndeath, and there it is!\nNow, tenderness: give battle with it, and then you prevail;",
   "v": true,
   "i": "to cast off frugality and go for reach, to cast off the last place and go for the first — that is death. Tenderness: fight with it and you win;",
   "n": "死矣 is two characters and a whole verdict: 'dead — and there it is'. 矣 does the sentencing.\n\nWang Bi on 夫慈以戰則勝: 相慜而不避於難 — men who feel tenderly towards one another do not shirk the danger, and that is why they win. The claim is not that gentleness disarms an enemy, but that it makes soldiers unwilling to abandon each other."
  },
